{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Author ADR 0106 defining **remote-anchored below-horizon HISTORY reclamation** whose PRIMARY lever\nis **commit/tree collapse** (retired-event GC is a secondary companion, not the pack lever), and\npromote docs/concurrency.md §I1 'permanent retention' (epic b306) from a follow-up note to an\nimplemented+cross-referenced model. This ADR is the causal-stability contract that unblocks S1-S3.\n(ADR number 0106 — 0105 was taken by an unrelated ADR that landed on origin/main.)\n\nScope (docs-only): the horizon config key (default 30d, portable, no CI-provider dependency); the\nremote-reachability computation (collapse checkpoint reachable from the sync remote's tickets ref\nfor >= N days); the stale-clone detection + FORCED remote-override protocol on reconnect (a clone\nwhose last convergence is older than N days overrides local with remote rather than reintroducing\npre-collapse history by rebase); the **C1-C5 causal-stability boundary at the commit/tree-rewrite\nlevel**; SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage OR enforce_since re-anchor for signature/authorship\nverifiability; the portable rewrite primitive and per-backend publish-swap; and a proof that\ninvariants I1-I9 still hold. State the accepted residual: a >N-day-drifted clone's divergent local\nwork is discarded. (Re-scoped 2026-08-29 from '.retired-only' to the commit/tree-collapse lever -\nsee epic comment 'Child-roster re-scope'.)\n\nNote: ADR numbering is a bijection — the ADR file is paired with a `docs/adr/.numbers/0106` marker\nand the generated `docs/adr/README.md` index, both DERIVED by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` from\n`docs/adr/*.md` and checked by `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` + `gen_adr_index.py --check` in the CI\ndocs-gates action (`.github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml`), NOT in `make lint`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` exists with the ADR shape (`# ADR 0106:`\n  title, `- **Status:**`, `## Context`, `## Decision`, `## Consequences`).\n- [ ] The ADR defines the N-day horizon as a portable config key (default 30d, with a stated rationale)\n  and NO single-CI-provider trigger (the `project.portability` criterion applies).\n- [ ] The ADR specifies remote-reachability (collapse checkpoint reachable from the sync remote tickets\n  ref for >= N days) and the stale-clone FORCED remote-override protocol on reconnect.\n- [ ] The ADR states the C1-C5 causal-stability boundary at the commit/tree-rewrite level and how\n  signature/authorship verifiability is preserved (SNAPSHOT authorship_ledger carriage AND enforce_since\n  re-anchor, both applied).\n- [ ] The ADR names the history-rewrite primitive as core-git (`git fast-import` / `mktree`+`commit-tree`,\n  NO third-party `git filter-repo`) and, per backend, the publish-swap: git-ref `--force-with-lease` CAS\n  for git remotes, and an exclusive push-locked bundle-set replacement bypassing the `git-remote-s3`\n  auto-doctor for the S3 backend — citing the auto-doctor never-discard-a-head resurrection hazard\n  (ADR 0093 / `src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py`) and proving its bypass safe under C1-C5.\n- [ ] The ADR proves invariants I1-I9 hold under reclamation and names the accepted residual\n  (>N-day-drifted clone divergent local work discarded).\n- [ ] The ADR-number bijection artifacts are regenerated: `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` creates the\n  `docs/adr/.numbers/0106` marker (content = the ADR filename) and adds a 0106 entry to the generated\n  `docs/adr/README.md` index; no ADR cross-reference dangles.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` §I1 is promoted from 'follow-up' to implemented and cross-references ADR 0106.\n\n## Verification\n- `test -f docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` and\n  `grep -n '^# ADR 0106:' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md` and\n  `grep -n '^## \\(Context\\|Decision\\|Consequences\\)' docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md`\n  confirm the ADR shape and title.\n- `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` then `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and\n  `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` pass (marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0106` present, README index\n  regenerated, bijection intact, no dangling cross-reference).\n- `grep -n 'ADR 0106\\|implemented' docs/concurrency.md` confirms the §I1 promotion wording and\n  cross-reference; `grep -n '0106' docs/adr/README.md` confirms the index entry.\n- `make lint` passes (ruff/format only); `rebar review-plan unlikely-zealous-skua` re-run confirms the\n  plan is admissible."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788049844463114871,"uuid":"6e510715-0693-4cb0-b770-051054be0c41"}